versity of New Hampshire at 55-38, and even a Republican-sponsored poll had him up seven. Raters unanimously call the race Solid or Safe Democratic, and markets price his win odds at 95 percent or better, so the incumbent's position in a D+8 state looks secure.", "watch": "A late external shock, such as an energy-price spike or a national wave breaking against Democrats, could tighten the race, but Fazio would need a shift far larger than any recent poll shows.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent Ned Lamont (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Governor Ned Lamont is seeking a third term against state Senator Ryan Fazio, and every available signal points to a comfortable Democratic hold. Polling since June has shown Lamont ahead by double digits in most surveys, including Quinnipiac and University of New Hampshire polls in September at 55-38; even a Republican-sponsored poll had him up seven. Averages of the polls put the lead near fifteen points.\n\nRaters across the spectrum call the race Solid or Safe Democratic, and prediction markets price Lamont's chances at 95 percent or higher. Fazio has campaigned on affordability and energy costs and has criticized Lamont's ties to utility Eversource, but there is little evidence the message has moved voters. Connecticut's Democratic lean and the incumbent's advantages frame this as one of the least competitive governor's races on the 2026 map.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.994, "margin": 15.28}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9913, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9896, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9893, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9879, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9857, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9868, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9861, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9879, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9889, "margin": 14.5}, {